# Test and push by default

After finishing a meaningful code change in this repo:

1. Run the relevant tests (at minimum the packages/areas you touched).
2. Commit the change with a concise message focused on why.
3. Push to the tracked remote branch (`git push` / `git push -u` when needed).

Do this without waiting to be asked, unless the user explicitly says not to commit or not to push.

Do not commit secrets, local screenshots, or unrelated junk files.
